          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சேமி — cēmi — \"to save up; to store\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நான் பயணத்துக்காகப் பணம் சேமித்தேன். nāṉ payaṇattukkākap paṇam cēmittēṉ. I saved money for the trip."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): சேமித்தேன், cēmittēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சேமிப்பு, savings, is its noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சேமி (cēmi) is usually traced to Sanskrit kṣema, \"safety, welfare\" (CDIAL 3745), through Tamil சேமம், \"safekeeping\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
